+7 Cleaver (1d8+1d6+1d4+7 [10-25] / 2d6+2d4+7 [11-27]) does comparable
damage to +7 Excalibur (1d8+1d10+7 [9-25] / 1d12+1d10+7 [9-29]).  So, a
barbarian flurrying Cleaver would get 20-50/22-54 damage.

Against non-demonic targets without appropriate resistances, the
Brand or GS combo (artifact + katana), does:
 (1d8+7)*2 + (1d10+7) = 16-30 + 8-17 = 24-47 (small)
 (1d8+7)*2 + (1d10+7) = 16-30 + 8-19 = 24-49 (large, using GS)
 (1d12+7)*2 + (1d12+7) = 16-38 + 8-19 = 24-57 (large, using brand)

Obviously, GS+ss will outperform any other combination against demons;
against things that resist their element, the brands will do 9-15/9-19
points less damage.

I have not analysed strength and skill bonuses, as those are applied
*after* all artifact bonuses are resolved.

Bear in mind also that a +7 tsurugi (yeah, I have to burn a wish on the
damn thing, or find a Samurai-Samurai double-bones file) can be used
with this ability; a +7 tsurugi does 8-23 (1d16+7) damage to small targets
and 10-27 (1d8+2d6+7) to large targets, for two-attack performance
figures (16-26 or 20-54) only marginally worse than Cleaver's.

I will note in passing that I am of the "#two-weapon is too powerful and
must be nerfed" school of thought, so you're definitely not going to
sell me Barbarians getting two attacks.

(My position is: #twoweapon should be for samurai and rogues only,
should be heavily penalised if you are using a weapon larger than a
short sword in your off hand, and should only produce a maximum of one
blow per attack action anyway.)

